<title>USA: U.N. sanctions panel to wait on Turkish oil.</title>
<headline>U.N. sanctions panel to wait on Turkish oil.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.N. Security Council sanctions committee decided Wednesday to delay a decision on a Turkish request for Iraqi oil until it sees how the still to be implemented oil-for-food accord operates, according to a diplomat on the sanction panel.</p>
<p>At the same Wednesday meeting, the committee also reviewed evidence of possible sanctions violations by Iran.</p>
<p>The diplomat said the U.S. charged Iran with aiding Iraq with smuggling oil in violation of U.N. sanctions prohibiting such actions.</p>
<p>&quot;Evidence will now be presented in written form as well, and then we will decide how to take it forward,&quot; said the sanctions committee member.</p>
</text>
